    },
    "body": "The retained model selected the correct value but copied it before the lexical suffix could place its owner first. Extend the existing signed-H4 lexical selector with learned Base, lexical byte/EOS, Owner-read and Value/span-read choices anchored to the exact inherited selected record. Explicit owner-first requests now freely emit ` selvi is in Dusk Ridge.\\n`, while the prior value-first, numeric and Rust behavior remains exact. No runtime phrase parser, sentence template, query-owner substitution or serving matrix product is introduced.\n\nThe artifact witness freezes the complete parent except new shared-selector transforms; removing the extension restores parent bytes exactly. Checkpoint schema /7 replays actual output to verify typed field state, and observed-token mismatch clears transient selection. Retain candidate d1b0985f at this bounded scope; the result and evidence record both unsuccessful preparations, complete resources and the next writer repair.\n\nValidation executed locally:\n- 80/80 construction answers and 30/30 post-selection fixed-form identity transfers; context/geometry/read interventions lose the new owner-first answers.\n- 873/873 inherited output/EOS/record comparisons, all 663 retained answers, earlier word/numeric panels, 12 exact histories and 14 exact semantic/control report comparisons.\n- 187 actual native API checks; 39 unique focused tests including the kernel source guard and eight actual-artifact zero-allocation/checkpoint checks.\n- Actual generated Rust equalities and four identifier-return fragments extracted, compiled and executed; release/offline builds, fmt and claim-wording checks passed.\n\nStructural stress is 12/14. Two revision cases expose the inherited writer storing `now` as an owner and failing to commit a revision; they remain explicit negatives. General prose, arbitrary instructions, Rust synthesis, frontier/alpha and energy advantage are unqualified. New-artifact browser/WASM/HTTP, full suite and Clippy were not run. GitHub's five historical status names acknowledge queue compatibility and execute no tests.\n\nResources: 1,890.025 model seconds and 551.511 engineering-command seconds; cumulative model 24,122.067 / 26,250 seconds. The necessary 1,200-second extension was recorded before use. Storage stays within its existing limit with the 128 MiB stop margin; no unique deletion or paid external compute.\n\nReferences #973\n",
